    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with the mathematics and their own captured worked solutions. Completing squares in q-165482 gives (y-1)^2/4-(x+2)^2/16=1, hence slopes ±1/2. The chain rule gives q-48763: 3(2)=6; q-48765: (6(-2)^2-2)(1)=22; q-48806: sqrt(2)/(-sin(pi/4))=-2; q-48801: cos(pi)(-3)=3; q-72231: (2(2)-6)(3)=-6 cm/s; q-115785: (12(3)^2+16)(-1/4)=-31 cm/s. The required three-term approximations give q-134609: 1-0.3+0.036=0.736 and q-178288: 1-0.07+0.0021=0.9321. For q-134534 and q-134536, the approximations are 30.432 and 212.328; their relative percentage errors are approximately 0.001046% and 0.021419%, rounding to 0.0% and 0.02%. In q-50607 the ratio is 3^(k-2), so convergence requires k<2. In q-124913 the ratios 2/3, -3/4, and 0.9 all have magnitude below one. In q-78445, (AB)^(-1)=B^(-1)A^(-1). For q-120896 the roots are approximately 2.461918 and 3.821267, whose product is approximately 9.408, rounding to 9. For q-3619 the partial-fraction coefficients are 4, -3, and 9, yielding the selected antiderivative. Two authored intermediate errors require a source_error judgment: q-48806 incorrectly writes dr/dt=(dtheta/dt)cos(theta) in its substitution block before correctly using -sin(theta); q-134609 incorrectly labels its left-hand side (0.94)^6 while calculating the requested fifth-power approximation. Neither error changes the source's final answer, so all answer disagreements are false.",
